The export contains 427 rows, but 15 repeat report IDs. Counting each report once leaves
**412 reports** merged into #4471. They do not describe one bug. Tenant locale and
booking-form version separate them into two problems.

## The split

| Problem | Reports | What breaks |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Shared parser | **379** | The parser reads month first, but day-first tenants expect day first. |
| Booking-v3 hint | **33** | The form shows `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants, so the hint and tenant date handling disagree. |

The parser reports span all 11 day-first tenants and app, email, and form channels. The hint
reports are form submissions from the three day-first tenants using booking-v3: alder.physio,
copper.studio, and pale.harbour.

## Intake tags are not causes

Intake tagged 356 parser reports `parser` and 23 `hint`. It tagged 18 hint reports `hint` and
15 `parser`. These labels are guesses, not independent problem counts: classify by tenant
locale, form version, and channel instead.

The desk's five one-day-move notes (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, and R-41620) all
belong to the parser group. Read them as evidence about reports filed under #4471, not as a
third cause.

